<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Sumich slides to year net loss.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Sumich slides to year net loss.</headline>
<dateline>PERTH 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30</p>
<p>		   (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		loss 4.09 vs profit 1.96</p>
<p>    Net				 loss 6.73 vs profit 1.38</p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)		nil vs 3.00</p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)		nil vs nil</p>
<p>    Sales				   96.91 vs 102.46</p>
<p>    Other income			   1.24 vs 1.23</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)		    loss 22.57 vs profit 4.66</p>
<p>    Abnormal items		  loss 4.86 vs nil</p>
<p>    Tax			     credit 2.23 vs expense 1.38</p>
<p>    Interest				 1.10 vs 0.92</p>
<p>    Depreciation			   3.03 vs 2.36</p>
<p>    Minorities				nil vs nil</p>
<p>NOTE: Sumich Group Ltd is a Western  Australian based horticultural group. On May 31 the company said it had expected a loss of about A$6 million before tax due to low values for produce and near record low prices for onions.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373 1800</p>
</text>
